To complete the Nimbus iQ AI ecosystem ("One Sovereign Core. Infinite Enterprise Verticals."), you elevate your Browser Agent into a full iQ Bot Computer Agent (@iq-computer)—a cross-domain, cross-platform autonomous desktop and terminal runtime.
While a browser agent is trapped inside a web viewport, an iQ Computer Agent controls an entire virtualized operating system (Linux/Windows/macOS desktop + root bash terminal + local filesystem + API bridge). This gives Nimbus iQ true cross-domain interoperability—allowing one agent to pull data from a legacy desktop app, transform it in a Python terminal, push it to a SaaS API, and verify it in a web browser within a single sovereign session.
Cross-Domain & Cross-Platform Architecture
To achieve seamless interoperability across terminals, native GUIs, web apps, and enterprise APIs, unify four execution planes under the Nimbus Sovereign Core:
Execution Plane	What It Controls	Enterprise Interoperability Role
Terminal & Shell Plane	Persistent bash / zsh / PowerShell, SSH tunnels, Docker CLI, Git, Python/Node runtimes	Executes scripts, manages servers, runs local ETL pipelines, and bridges internal VPC networks.
GUI Desktop Plane (Computer Use)	Full X11 / Wayland virtual display (1920x1080) via VNC/WebRTC, mouse (x, y), keyboard, clipboard	Operates legacy Windows/Linux thick clients, Excel spreadsheets, SAP GUI, and OS settings without APIs.
Headless Browser Plane	Chromium + Playwright + CDP Screencast	Handles modern web portals, OAuth logins, DOM scraping, and live web app QA.
MCP & API Interop Bus	Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers, REST/GraphQL, gRPC, SQL/Snowflake connectors	Connects structured enterprise cloud tools (Slack, Jira, Salesforce, Postgres) directly to local terminal files.
How to Source the Computer & Terminal Runtime
You do not need to build virtual desktop streaming from scratch. Combine these infrastructure primitives:
• Cloud Desktop & Terminal Sandboxes: E2B Desktop Sandbox (@e2b/desktop), Anthropic Computer Use Reference Container (Docker + Xvfb + xdotool + scrot), or Kasm Workspaces (for enterprise VDI streaming).
• Live Interactive Streaming: noVNC or WebRTC embedded in your Next.js right-hand pane so users can watch the terminal and desktop live—and click "Take Control" anytime.
• Cross-Platform Relay (Local-to-Cloud Bridge): An optional lightweight Nimbus Sovereign Daemon (written in Go or Rust) that enterprises install on on-prem Windows/macOS/Linux machines to expose local terminals safely over mTLS without opening inbound firewall ports.
